cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "qecscreen: circuit-level screening for quantum LDPC code search"
message: "If you use this software or its dataset, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Pushkar
    affiliation: "MIT Art, Design and Technology University, Pune, India"
    # FILL: add your ORCID once registered at https://orcid.org (free, 2 minutes).
    # An ORCID is what disambiguates you from every other Pushkar Kumar in the
    # literature, and it is the single cheapest thing you can do for credit.
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    # FILL: email you are willing to publish
    # email: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pushkar0997/qecscreen"  # FILL if renamed
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.0.1
date-released: "2026-08-30"
keywords:
  - quantum error correction
  - quantum LDPC codes
  - machine learning
  - benchmark
  - surrogate model
abstract: >-
  Measured circuit-level logical error rates for bivariate bicycle (BB)
  quantum LDPC codes with n <= 72 (Stim circuits decoded with BP+OSD under one
  pinned protocol), and a baseline for evaluating cheap screening scores, such
  as the code-level proxy Φ = kd^2/n, against them.

